A small downside is that this circuit is open loop.

497
00:38:21,650 --> 00:38:25,050
If you leave it without load, high potential can build up here.

498
00:38:27,270 --> 00:38:29,570
Significantly above 350V.

499
00:38:31,270 --> 00:38:34,550
I took a 450V capacitor, that's enough.

500
00:38:36,610 --> 00:38:38,830
But I'll tinker with this circuit a bit more.

501
00:38:41,010 --> 00:38:43,630
I'll lay out this circuit, then show how it works.

502
00:38:44,870 --> 00:38:47,130
This chip has one wonderful property.

503
00:38:48,130 --> 00:38:54,330
If you apply logical zero to pin 3, simply apply minus of the power source, it stops generation.

504
00:38:55,170 --> 00:38:57,770
I think on this principle you can make voltage feedback.

505
00:38:59,290 --> 00:39:03,530
For example, to hold 330VDC at the output.

506
00:39:04,870 --> 00:39:08,930
The cap reaches 330V and the chip stops generation.

507
00:39:10,290 --> 00:39:13,170
I'll make something simple, then I'll share the schematic.

508
00:39:14,710 --> 00:39:19,370
Marking here, before I print this schematic, sending it to my Yandex disk.

509
00:39:21,090 --> 00:39:24,150
I'll mark the Her5O8 diodes too.

510
00:39:25,510 --> 00:39:26,610
And basically that's all.

